<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Luna-Lift-Reader: Lares (Tasked Spirit). A cold read, read-only, of a design carrier against the operator's rulings.
Read `git -C /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/b1-lift/wt show 5c7b8cbc2:bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/browser-vessel-lift.mem` and the road at the same SHA: `...:bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem` (#/rulings: PAGE NEVER A VESSEL 2026-10-29; custody by capability never host 2026-10-19; the browser rulings ~227-233; "a shared act never makes a shared secret" ~235-238; row B1; X0b) and `...:bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom.mem`.
Rulings arriving 2026-11-05 to check the carrier against: "Browser + Node is part of founding" (the lift rises before the rite); "Land all before the rite, no 'build a now, b later'"; "Multiple tabs will carry live sessions, and later can change face (one face per session)"; "realm" stays reserved for the DreamNet concept (say thread for a JavaScript execution context).
CHECK: (1) does every slice keep each ruling (no key or seed or route on the page after the cut; each tab its own unlock and live session; the last tab returns the browser to its floor; one owner per store; custody named by capability, never by host); (2) any slice or reading that defers design work past the rite; (3) the house readings (4 items) — does any contradict a ruling's text (quote both); (4) the port message list: anything sovereign still crossing to the page; (5) internal contradictions between slots; (6) L-Prime and evergreen prose; "realm" used only for the DreamNet.
Output (final message, under 650 words): findings with slot names and line numbers, each tagged RULING / DEFERRAL / CONTRADICTION / L-PRIME / REALM, plus a verdict.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

